{"items":[
{"label":"2A","direction":"supports","claim":"After removing duplicate amendment rows, PHAC's Illumina contract value fell about 76% from fiscal 2024-25 to fiscal 2025-26, and its order count fell about 73%.","detail":"The Public Health Agency of Canada (PHAC; it runs the National Microbiology Lab) contracts with ILLUMINA CANADA ULC were summed on Canada's April-to-March fiscal year. FY24-25 was about C$7.32M on 120 orders (Apr–Jun 2024 C$1.28M + H2'24 C$3.49M + Jan–Mar 2025 C$2.54M). FY25-26 was about C$1.76M on 33 orders (Apr–Jun 2025 C$0.078M + H2'25 C$0.734M + Jan–Mar 2026 C$0.948M). The FY25-26 figure counts the Feb 2026 C$630K equipment procurement only once, at its amended C$644.8K value. Calendar 2024 totals C$7.26M on 120 orders, against C$3.35M on 64 orders in 2025. The 2025 figure reconciles with the known ~C$3.4M.","url":"https://open.canada.ca/data/en/api/action/datastore_search?resource_id=fac950c0-00d5-4ec1-a4d3-9cbebf98a305&filters=%7B%22vendor_name%22%3A%22ILLUMINA%20CANADA%20ULC%22%2C%22owner_org_title%22%3A%22Public%20Health%20Agency%20of%20Canada%20%7C%20Agence%20de%20la%20sant%C3%A9%20publique%20du%20Canada%22%7D&limit=400&fields=reference_number,contract_date,contract_value&sort=contract_date%20desc","date":"2026-06-29","source_name":"Government of Canada Proactive Disclosure of Contracts (open.canada.ca)","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"strong","why_new":"F448 gave calendar 2022/2025 values only; this is a deduplicated fiscal-year series with order counts, including FY25-26."},
{"label":"2A","direction":"supports","claim":"F452's flat H1 2026 reading double-counts one PHAC contract. Deduplicated, PHAC's Illumina spend fell about 53% y/y in H1'26.","detail":"Procurement 6D06353301 shows up twice: C-2025-2026-Q4-00424 (C$630,439, type C) and C-2025-2026-Q4-00425 (C$644,850, type A). The second row is an amendment whose contract_value is cumulative (C$630,439 + C$14,410). Counted once, PHAC H1'26 is C$1.244M on 20 orders, against C$2.621M on 46 orders in H1'25 (−53% in value, −57% in orders). If the earlier ~C$3.19M all-federal H1'26 total added both rows, the corrected figure is about C$2.55M, or about −22% vs C$3.29M rather than −3%.","url":"https://open.canada.ca/data/en/api/action/datastore_search?resource_id=fac950c0-00d5-4ec1-a4d3-9cbebf98a305&filters=%7B%22vendor_name%22%3A%5B%22ILLUMINA%20CANADA%20ULC%22%2C%22ILLUMINA%20CANADA%20INC%22%2C%22ILLUMINA%20CANADA%20INC.%22%2C%22ILLUMINA%2C%20INC.%22%5D%2C%22instrument_type%22%3A%22A%22%7D&limit=100","date":"2026-02-04","source_name":"Government of Canada Proactive Disclosure of Contracts","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"strong","why_new":"Corrects F452. Amendment rows (instrument_type A) repeat the cumulative value and were not removed before."},
{"label":"1C","direction":"supports","claim":"Excluding instrument purchases, consumable-type Illumina spend at PHAC and AAFC fell 70–77% y/y in H1 2026. The headline is propped up by new instruments.","detail":"PHAC H1'26 without the C$644.8K equipment buy is C$0.599M, against C$2.621M in H1'25 (−77%); all H1'25 PHAC rows were 'Medical supplies'/lab supplies. At Agriculture and Agri-Food Canada (AAFC), H1'26 without the C$404.9K instrument is C$108.8K on 8 orders, against C$364.5K on 20 orders in H1'25 (−70%). About C$1.45M of the deduplicated ~C$2.55M federal H1'26 total (~57%) is three instrument buys: Health Canada C$404.9K, AAFC C$404.9K and PHAC C$644.8K.","url":"https://open.canada.ca/data/en/api/action/datastore_search?resource_id=fac950c0-00d5-4ec1-a4d3-9cbebf98a305&filters=%7B%22vendor_name%22%3A%5B%22ILLUMINA%20CANADA%20ULC%22%2C%22ILLUMINA%20CANADA%20INC%22%2C%22ILLUMINA%20CANADA%20INC.%22%2C%22ILLUMINA%2C%20INC.%22%5D%2C%22owner_org_title%22%3A%5B%22Agriculture%20and%20Agri-Food%20Canada%20%7C%20Agriculture%20et%20Agroalimentaire%20Canada%22%2C%22Health%20Canada%20%7C%20Sant%C3%A9%20Canada%22%5D%7D&limit=150","date":"2026-06-30","source_name":"Government of Canada Proactive Disclosure of Contracts","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"strong","why_new":"First split of federal Illumina spend into instruments and consumables. F452 treated H1'26 as one flat total."},
{"label":"2A","direction":"supports","claim":"PHAC's year-end (Jan–Mar) Illumina reagent buying collapsed by about 88% in 2026.","detail":"Federal departments usually spend leftover budget before the 31 March fiscal year-end. PHAC's Jan–Mar Illumina buying was C$2.49M in 2024 and C$2.54M in 2025 (42 orders, including call-ups of C$394K, C$254K, C$230K, C$134K and C$132K). In 2026 the same window had only C$0.303M of supplies on 10 orders, plus the C$644.8K equipment procurement. Without that equipment, the decline is −88% y/y.","url":"https://open.canada.ca/data/en/api/action/datastore_search?resource_id=fac950c0-00d5-4ec1-a4d3-9cbebf98a305&filters=%7B%22vendor_name%22%3A%22ILLUMINA%20CANADA%20ULC%22%2C%22owner_org_title%22%3A%22Public%20Health%20Agency%20of%20Canada%20%7C%20Agence%20de%20la%20sant%C3%A9%20publique%20du%20Canada%22%7D&limit=400&fields=reference_number,contract_date,contract_value&sort=contract_date%20desc","date":"2026-03-31","source_name":"Government of Canada Proactive Disclosure of Contracts","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"F451 covered Oct–Dec only. The fiscal year-end budget flush is a separate, larger signal."},
{"label":"2A","direction":"supports","claim":"PHAC's large-order Illumina channel through standing offer CW2237770 went quiet for 12.5 months, and orders of C$100K or more fell from 21 (2024) to 8 (2025) to 1 (H1'26).","detail":"Call-ups against standing offer CW2237770 (a pre-negotiated government supply agreement; all Illumina, all PHAC) were C$2.01M across 21 orders in 2024. There were none between 31 Oct 2024 and 18 Nov 2025, then 2 orders worth C$0.25M in 2025 and 2 worth C$0.21M in H1'26 (C$63.6K and C$150.9K). Across all PHAC Illumina contracts, orders of C$100K or more fell from 21 in 2024 to 8 in 2025 to 1 consumables order in H1'26 (C$150.9K, 13 May 2026). The many small C$20–25K orders largely continue.","url":"https://open.canada.ca/data/en/api/action/datastore_search?resource_id=fac950c0-00d5-4ec1-a4d3-9cbebf98a305&filters=%7B%22standing_offer_number%22%3A%5B%22CW2237770%22%2C%226D063-224285%22%5D%7D&limit=200","date":"2026-05-13","source_name":"Government of Canada Proactive Disclosure of Contracts","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"F457 covered only small monthly orders. The large-order collapse and the standing-offer gap are new."},
{"label":"2A","direction":"against","claim":"Much of PHAC's decline is the end of COVID-era genomic surveillance, not switching to rivals or price pressure.","detail":"PHAC's procurement 6D06304822 (Illumina, 'Medical supplies') was a C$15.40M reagent contract dated 4 Jun 2021, amended by +C$3.88M to C$19.28M, with delivery through 31 May 2023. That single pandemic contract is about 2.5x PHAC's full FY24-25 Illumina spend. Most of the multi-year drop is therefore normalization after the pandemic surveillance build-out, so it is a weak read on Illumina pricing or share.","url":"https://open.canada.ca/data/en/api/action/datastore_search?resource_id=fac950c0-00d5-4ec1-a4d3-9cbebf98a305&filters=%7B%22vendor_name%22%3A%5B%22ILLUMINA%20CANADA%20ULC%22%2C%22ILLUMINA%20CANADA%20INC%22%2C%22ILLUMINA%20CANADA%20INC.%22%2C%22ILLUMINA%2C%20INC.%22%5D%2C%22instrument_type%22%3A%22A%22%7D&limit=100","date":"2021-06-04","source_name":"Government of Canada Proactive Disclosure of Contracts","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"strong","why_new":"The COVID master contract was not in F447–F460 and changes how the decline should be read."},
{"label":"2A","direction":"against","claim":"Earlier federal baselines were inflated by duplicate amendment rows, so the measured 2022→2025 and 2024→2025 declines are overstated.","detail":"Several contracts appear more than once with the same contract date. PHAC service contract 6D06315510 appears at C$2.80M and at C$2.88M (cumulative), both dated 29 Aug 2022. PHAC equipment 6D06325263 appears at C$609K and at C$850K, both dated 10 Feb 2023. CFIA 20240441A appears as an original row (~C$1.00M) plus two amendment rows (C$0.40M and C$1.21M), all dated 5 Mar 2024; AAFC and Health Canada have smaller cases. If those baselines were summed naively, PHAC 2022 (~C$9.6M) is overstated by ~C$2.8M (true ~C$6.8M, so ~−51% to 2025, not −65%), and 2024 all-federal is overstated by ~C$1.5M.","url":"https://open.canada.ca/data/en/api/action/datastore_search?resource_id=fac950c0-00d5-4ec1-a4d3-9cbebf98a305&filters=%7B%22vendor_name%22%3A%22ILLUMINA%20CANADA%20ULC%22%2C%22reference_number%22%3A%5B%22C-2022-2023-Q2-00482%22%2C%22C-2024-2025-Q4-00487%22%2C%22C-2022-2023-Q4-00814%22%2C%22C-2023-2024-Q2-00434%22%5D%7D&limit=20","date":"2022-08-29","source_name":"Government of Canada Proactive Disclosure of Contracts","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"Methodology correction to F447/F448 baselines."},
{"label":"2A","direction":"against","claim":"The federal trough may be behind: PHAC's Apr–Jun 2026 Illumina spend nearly quadrupled y/y, and NRC's H1'26 already exceeds its full 2025.","detail":"PHAC Apr–Jun 2026 was C$0.296M on 9 orders, against C$0.078M on 4 orders in Apr–Jun 2025 (+280%). That includes a C$150.9K call-up on 13 May 2026, the first consumables order over C$100K since Dec 2025. National Research Council (NRC) Illumina orders were C$580K (21 orders) in 2022, C$293K (13) in 2023, C$120K (7) in 2024 and C$57K (3) in 2025. In H1'26 NRC already had C$74K (3 orders).","url":"https://open.canada.ca/data/en/api/action/datastore_search?resource_id=fac950c0-00d5-4ec1-a4d3-9cbebf98a305&filters=%7B%22vendor_name%22%3A%5B%22ILLUMINA%20CANADA%20ULC%22%2C%22ILLUMINA%20CANADA%20INC%22%2C%22ILLUMINA%20CANADA%20INC.%22%2C%22ILLUMINA%2C%20INC.%22%5D%2C%22owner_org_title%22%3A%22National%20Research%20Council%20Canada%20%7C%20Conseil%20national%20de%20recherches%20Canada%22%7D&limit=200&fields=contract_date,contract_value,instrument_type,description_en&sort=contract_date%20desc","date":"2026-06-29","source_name":"Government of Canada Proactive Disclosure of Contracts","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"F449 gave only NRC's 2022–25 decline. The Q2'26 PHAC and H1'26 NRC rebound is new."},
{"label":"2B","direction":"against","claim":"Federal labs are still buying new Illumina instruments without competition in 2025-26, including two at an identical C$404,866.81 price.","detail":"Health Canada (HT28253534, 30 Jan 2026) and AAFC (20260485A, 17 Feb 2026) each bought Illumina equipment for exactly C$404,866.81. Both were non-competitive (TN) with one bid, which points to a uniform government price rather than case-by-case discounting. Other recent buys: AAFC C$276,132 (25 Sep 2025, limited-tendering reason 71) and Health Canada C$158,258 (24 Dec 2025). Together with PHAC's C$644.8K, that is about C$1.89M of Illumina instrument capital in five months. No matching Element or Ultima instrument award appears in this window.","url":"https://open.canada.ca/data/en/api/action/datastore_search?resource_id=fac950c0-00d5-4ec1-a4d3-9cbebf98a305&filters=%7B%22vendor_name%22%3A%5B%22ILLUMINA%20CANADA%20ULC%22%2C%22ILLUMINA%20CANADA%20INC%22%2C%22ILLUMINA%20CANADA%20INC.%22%5D%2C%22contract_value%22%3A%5B404866.81%2C276132.46%2C158257.86%2C561764.7%2C12625.04%2C24040.8%5D%7D&limit=20","date":"2026-02-17","source_name":"Government of Canada Proactive Disclosure of Contracts","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"F455/F456 covered the PHAC C$630K and CFIA 2024 buys only. The HC/AAFC 2025-26 instrument wave and identical pricing are new."},
{"label":"1B","direction":"against","claim":"Repeat federal Illumina orders show flat nominal prices for years, with only a ~1.2% step down at PHAC in Dec 2024.","detail":"AAFC bought a C$24,040.80 chemicals order (commodity 6810) on both 16 Jan 2024 and 17 Jan 2025. AAFC's C$23,445.24 order recurs 8 times from Oct 2019 to Jan 2023. C$24,848.25 recurs at NRC (6 times, Feb 2022–Jan 2023; plus C$49,696.50 = 2x in Feb 2021 and Jan 2023) and at AAFC (Mar and Nov 2022). PHAC's monthly C$23,930.55 order (6 times, Jun–Nov 2024) became C$23,649.00 (Dec 2024–Jan 2025, 3 times) and C$23,648.99/23,648.59 (Feb and Oct 2025), −1.2%. Caveat: SKUs are not disclosed, and orders may be sized to a C$25K sole-source threshold.","url":"https://open.canada.ca/data/en/api/action/datastore_search?resource_id=fac950c0-00d5-4ec1-a4d3-9cbebf98a305&filters=%7B%22vendor_name%22%3A%5B%22ILLUMINA%20CANADA%20ULC%22%2C%22ILLUMINA%20CANADA%20INC%22%2C%22ILLUMINA%20CANADA%20INC.%22%2C%22ILLUMINA%2C%20INC.%22%5D%2C%22owner_org_title%22%3A%5B%22Agriculture%20and%20Agri-Food%20Canada%20%7C%20Agriculture%20et%20Agroalimentaire%20Canada%22%2C%22Health%20Canada%20%7C%20Sant%C3%A9%20Canada%22%5D%7D&limit=150","date":"2025-10-08","source_name":"Government of Canada Proactive Disclosure of Contracts","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"First repeat-order unit-price series from this dataset (strategist question 3)."},
{"label":"1B","direction":"against","claim":"Illumina service contracts at federal labs renew at flat or higher prices, with no sign of service discounting.","detail":"AAFC renewed an Illumina repair/maintenance contract (commodity JX66) at exactly C$12,625.04 on 17 Feb 2025 (to Mar 2026) and again on 4 Feb 2026 (to Mar 2027). Health Canada paid C$25,929.32 a year on each of two service contracts (4500415550 and 4500418242), renewed unchanged 2020–2025. In Dec 2024 these were replaced by HT28246602 at C$57,039, about 10% above the C$51,859 combined, later amended to C$88,728 (to Jan 2026). ECCC's renewals held at C$37,203.89 a year from 2022 to 2025.","url":"https://open.canada.ca/data/en/api/action/datastore_search?resource_id=fac950c0-00d5-4ec1-a4d3-9cbebf98a305&filters=%7B%22vendor_name%22%3A%5B%22ILLUMINA%20CANADA%20ULC%22%2C%22ILLUMINA%20CANADA%20INC%22%2C%22ILLUMINA%20CANADA%20INC.%22%2C%22ILLUMINA%2C%20INC.%22%5D%2C%22instrument_type%22%3A%22A%22%7D&limit=100","date":"2026-02-04","source_name":"Government of Canada Proactive Disclosure of Contracts","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"Service-renewal pricing was not covered in F447–F460."},
{"label":"1A","direction":"against","claim":"PHAC's sole-source Illumina fleet service contract runs to 31 Aug 2027 and was enlarged in early 2025, so the legacy fleet is under service for at least another year.","detail":"Procurement 6D06315510 is a repair and maintenance contract for lab instruments: C$2.80M, 29 Aug 2022 to 31 Aug 2027 (about C$0.56M a year), limited-tendering reason 71, one bid. An amendment of +C$126.6K was reported in FY24-25 Q4, bringing it to C$2.88M. The instruments are not named, so this does not show 6000s specifically. It does commit the National Microbiology Lab's pandemic-era Illumina fleet to service through mid-2027.","url":"https://open.canada.ca/data/en/api/action/datastore_search?resource_id=fac950c0-00d5-4ec1-a4d3-9cbebf98a305&filters=%7B%22vendor_name%22%3A%22ILLUMINA%20CANADA%20ULC%22%2C%22reference_number%22%3A%5B%22C-2022-2023-Q2-00482%22%2C%22C-2024-2025-Q4-00487%22%5D%7D&limit=20","date":"2025-03-31","source_name":"Government of Canada Proactive Disclosure of Contracts","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"Answers strategist question 2 on service renewals. Not in F447–F460."},
{"label":"2B","direction":"supports","claim":"PacBio long-read purchases at Canadian agriculture labs held steady through 2024–26 while those labs' Illumina consumable buying fell.","detail":"AAFC bought PacBio at an identical C$21,864.00 five times (Mar 2024–Feb 2025), and the Canadian Grain Commission (CGC) bought C$18–24K PacBio orders through 19 Jan 2026. CGC also bought a C$679K PacBio instrument in Mar 2022. PacBio federal orders totaled about C$144K in 2024 and about C$130K in 2025, roughly flat. Over the same period AAFC's Illumina non-instrument spend fell 70% y/y in H1'26.","url":"https://open.canada.ca/data/en/api/action/datastore_search?resource_id=fac950c0-00d5-4ec1-a4d3-9cbebf98a305&q=%7B%22vendor_name%22%3A%22pacific%20biosciences%22%7D&limit=100","date":"2026-01-19","source_name":"Government of Canada Proactive Disclosure of Contracts","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"Canadian federal PacBio spend was not covered. Earlier items covered ONT, Element and MGI only."}
